  "details": "If you take a VRC+ print and position your avatar to stand behind the new VRC+ print with a first-person view facing away from the print, when you switch to third-person mode to view the print from behind the avatar using third-person view camera the print will be in low quality (optimized away).\n\nI expected to be able to view my print in full detail from the third-person view camera close-up, including the print details.\n\n- Photo 1: The print itself\n\n- Photo 2: The print viewed in first-person view (third-person view disabled)\n\n- Photo 3: The print viewed from third-person view while the avatar is standing behind the print and facing away from it",
